                "_type": "Diesel Product Detail",
                "about": {
                    "image": {
                        "src": "https://cdn2.unrealengine.com/egs-amongthesleepenhancededition-krillbitestudioas-s2-1200x1600-5df5441a776a.jpg",
                        "_type": "Diesel Image"
                    },
                    "developerAttribution": "Krillbite Studio AS",
                    "_type": "Diesel Product About",
                    "publisherAttribution": "Krillbite Studio AS",
                    "description": "Among the Sleep is a first person horror adventure, in which you play a two year old child. After waking up in the middle of the night to mysterious sounds, you start exploring the dark looking for comfort.\n\nThe game explores horror through atmosphere and exploration, not with scores and combat systems. In Among the Sleep you’re vulnerable, scared, and trying to make sense of the world.\n\nController support: Works 100% with Xbox 360 controllers, might have some issues with Xbox One controllers. We are sorry about the inconvience.\n\n# What people are saying:\n\n- _\"More, please!\" _\n [Kotaku](http://kotaku.com/5914081/a-horror-game-in-which-you-play-as-a-two-year-old)\n\n- _\"... it more than succeeds in creating a wonderfully eerie atmosphere full of childlike anxiety, and along the way tackles a serious subject in a darkly poignant manner.\"_\n[IGN][http://www.ign.com/articles/2014/06/05/among-the-sleep-review/]\n\n- _\"Its depiction of a first-person horror told through the eyes and stumbling little legs of a two-year old is as intriguing as anything I've seen all year, and reminiscent of a time when games actively sought out new ways to play and new stories to tell.\"_\n[Eurogamer][http://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2012-07-03-among-the-sleep-preview-they-mostly-come-at-night]\n\n# Awards\n\n**Winner of Nordic Game Awards - Best Artistic Achievement 2015**\n\n**Winner of the Nordic Indie Sensation 2014**\n\n**Winner of Momocon Indie Game Awards - Best Game 2015**\n\n**Nominated for Best Game Audio - Indie Prize Europe 2015**\n\n**Norwegian game of the year 2014, by Gamereactor**\n\n# Reviews\n\n- [The Guardian][http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2014/jun/16/among-the-sleep-review-childhood] 8/10 \"Among the Sleep deserves a great deal of credit for its story.\"\n\n- [Joystiq][http://www.joystiq.com/2014/05/29/among-the-sleep-review-real-monsters/] 8/10 \"You can never trust what's real and what's you being a scared little kid.\"\n\n- [Game Informer][http://www.gameinformer.com/games/among_the_sleep/b/pc/archive/2014/05/30/game-informer-review-among-the-sleep-pc.aspx] 7.8/10 \"It leaves more of an impact in a distilled 3 to 4 hours than some games with 60-hour campaigns.\"",
                    "shortDescription": "Among the Sleep: Enhanced Edition is a new and improved version of the award winning first person horror adventure. In the game you play as a small child trapped in a weird nightmare where you go looking for your mom.",
                    "title": "Among the Sleep - Enhanced Edition",
